ok to h3  is checkmate the black king has no  squares  so uh after this rook the d3 of course  uh boucher  said all right maybe the queen can be  captured just yet i'm gonna play king to  h5 now uh but now morphe just goes for  queen to f7 with check king to h4  and now rook the h3 with check king to  g4  and now queen to h5 and this is now  checkmate and we reached the position  from the thumbnail  and now you know how such a such a  position can even occur because if  someone just shows you this it's like  how did this king get here i mean which  path did he take i mean this is covered  you can't touch the g6 square how did  how did the king get the g4 but now you  know  uh and uh i mean what i mean this is  just a brilliant brilliant game  and uh you know uh definitely one for  the for the history books and it of  course  is featured in most of history books  that feature more of his games  but it's really really amazing uh how  morphy could create such masterpieces  you know  while playing blindfold against players  of reasonable you know  reasonable strength so  that's uh the game hope you guys enjoyed  that that's already the third game we've  shown from the blindfold simultaneous  exhibition we are going to  show some more as they are quite quite  enjoyable uh so hope you're ready for  that uh i would like to thank  uh mao mara mao unleashes alex s  mahendra tribune surah  yagadesh gunapanamath and please don't  mention my name for a contribution to my  channel thank you a lot i really  appreciate it  uh as usual you can check two of my  previous videos here thank you all for  watching  and i will see you soon continuing the  coverage of the morphe saga  uh checking up on your wonderful  suggestions and whatever else happens in  the chess world  uh so thank you all i will see you soon  and have an excellent rest of your day

